<title>UK: British Gas year profits fall.</title>
<headline>British Gas year profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>				 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		14.4		   vs 20.7</p>
<p> Current cost profit    641		    vs 909</p>
<p> Turnover		   9,453		  vs 8,601</p>
<p>NOTE - Above current cost profit is on a historical, pre-exceptional basis. Excluding minority interests, the results were 631 million stg versus 903 million stg.</p>
<p>Current cost profit on a post-exceptional basis fell to a loss of 571 million stg versus a profit of 130 million stg.</p>
<p>BG Plc proposed a final dividend of 8.1p, bringing the total for the year to 14.5p per share.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
